# Outputs, not tooling.
#
# BUILD-LAW's test for what gets committed is whether someone could re-derive
# it from the documents alone. The scripts in here, no: they implement a
# threshold and a window that the prose only describes. Their screenshots and
# JSON, yes — by running them. So the harness is tracked and what it prints is
# not, and a stale sweep from three builds ago never gets mistaken for a
# current measurement.
*.png
*.json

# out/ wholesale, because it is 41 MB and it holds contact sheets as well as
# frames, and .html is caught by neither rule above.
out/

# EXCEPT evidence/, and it is the one exception this file gets.
#
# Those frames show shapes that were built, measured, rejected, and whose code
# has since been DELETED — two hero entrances and two page transitions. The
# test above is "could someone re-derive this by running the script", and for
# these the answer is no: there is no longer a script, a switch or a stylesheet
# that produces them. They are the only pictures in here that a re-run cannot
# bring back, which is exactly why they are the only ones kept.
!evidence/
!evidence/*.png
